    "languages": [],
    "summaryAr": "3D Environment Artist & Level Designer ScapeWorld Entertainment · Remote Level: Senior to lead Location: Remote, CET overlap Contract: Full time, long term About us We are ScapeWorld Entertainment, a fully remote Swedish game studio of just over 20 people. We are building Scape, a platform of multiplayer games where a player’s identity carries across all of them. We have just launched our first game within Scape. Our",
    "descriptionAr": "3D Environment Artist & Level Designer ScapeWorld Entertainment · Remote Level: Senior to lead Location: Remote, CET overlap Contract: Full time, long term About us We are ScapeWorld Entertainment, a fully remote Swedish game studio of just over 20 people. We are building Scape, a platform of multiplayer games where a player’s identity carries across all of them. We have just launched our first game within Scape. Our senior team has shipped and run live games at studios including Arrowhead (Helldivers 2), Avalanche Studios and Ubisoft. The project Our next game is a cleaning and restoration sim set in a shared neighbourhood. Every player has a place of their own that starts buried in junk and grime, and puts it in order in full view of neighbours who are doing the same. Cleaning games are usually played alone or in short co-op sessions. We want to make one set in a neighbourhood that players share and keep coming back to, and we want to do it well. We have a working prototype and are refining the loop now. If you play games like this and have views on what makes them satisfying, you will enjoy this. About the role We are looking for a senior to lead 3D environment artist who is also a level designer. You will be the only level designer on the project. You own the game’s spaces, from first layout through to dressed and lit, and you are responsible for delivering them. The role is split roughly evenly between environment art, mostly props and other environment 3D assets, and level design, which includes some gameplay design. On the design side you work with our Creative Director and engineering, and you bring your level and gameplay design experience into those discussions. On the art side you work with the rest of the art team. You report to the Art Director. What you will do Environment art Model and texture props and other environment 3D assets. Most of what we use is made in-house, and we also work with asset packs where they fit. Work to our polygon, texture and material standards. Assets used in large numbers, such as foliage, are kept low poly. Most props use standard poly counts. Build modular kits that can be reused across levels. Dress and light levels in Unity, following the Art Director’s visual direction. Level design Design the layout of rooms and plots: how the player moves through them, what they notice first, and the order in which the space is revealed as it is cleared. Greybox levels and take them through to final, checking scale, pathing and collision in engine. Test levels in engine and in playtests, and make changes based on the results. Help shape how spaces support the game loop and its features, and give input on pacing and progression. Document your work: layout plans, kit guides and dressing guidelines. What we are looking for Senior to lead level, with several years of professional experience in game development. Experience as both an environment artist and a level designer. You have done each on at least one project, shipped or not, and you have owned a game’s spaces or levels from start to finish. Some gameplay design experience, for example working on game loops, features or mechanics alongside level layouts. A portfolio that shows both sides: real-time environments and 3D assets you made, and levels you designed, from greybox to final. Good working knowledge of Unity, including building and lighting levels. Our level tools are built inside Unity. Comfortable using Blender. It is part of our production pipeline, and we have built an add-on for it. Comfortable using the Substance suite for texturing and materials. Comfortable giving your view in design discussions and explaining your reasoning. Able to work independently from a brief, and to work closely with a small team. Comfortable working in English every day, in meetings (mostly on camera) and in writing. It does not need to be perfect. Nice to have 3D character or gameplay animation. 3D character modelling. Technical art or VFX. Experience with GitHub or Fork. Experience with player-built levels, or tools for game creators. Experience in a small team where you covered more than one role. What we offer A fully remote team with flexible working. Trust to manage your own time. We do not use timesheets. Ownership of the game’s spaces, from first layout to final. A small team where people help each other. Working setup Fully remote. Your working day needs to overlap with CET. Full time, on a long-term contract. It is business to business. We would like you to start as soon as you are available. What this role is not Not a lead game designer role. Our Creative Director sets the direction of the game. Not an art-only or design-only role. You will do both. How to apply Apply through the link; a few short questions are part of the application form. If we shortlist you, the next step is interviews, and for final candidates an unpaid planning task of about two hours at an agreed time, with no modelling or texturing. We reply to everyone at every step. Disclosure This application will be evaluated with the help of an AI tool that checks your CV and application against the criteria for this role. A human recruiter always makes the final decision. The AI does not reject or accept anyone on its own. If your application isn’t taken forward, you can ask us for an explanation of how the AI was used in that decision. See our Candidate Privacy Policy below for full details, or contact us at Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow",
