    "languages": [],
    "summaryAr": "Perplexity is seeking a Regional Sales Director to build and lead our Legal vertical. You'll own the number for law firms and in-house legal teams, hire and lead a team of Account Executives and set the go-to-market strategy for how Perplexity Enterprise shows up in the legal profession. You'll help firms and legal departments research faster, work from trusted and cited sources, and bring AI into confidential, high-",
    "descriptionAr": "Perplexity is seeking a Regional Sales Director to build and lead our Legal vertical. You'll own the number for law firms and in-house legal teams, hire and lead a team of Account Executives and set the go-to-market strategy for how Perplexity Enterprise shows up in the legal profession. You'll help firms and legal departments research faster, work from trusted and cited sources, and bring AI into confidential, high-stakes work with the security and governance they expect. This role is ideal for a builder who has sold AI or legal technology to the most demanding firms and GCs, knows how legal organizations evaluate and roll out new tools, and wants to build a vertical from the ground up. Responsibilities Own the Legal vertical number across AmLaw and global law firms and in-house legal teams at large enterprises Build the vertical go-to-market strategy, including target accounts, segmentation, territory design, pricing input and a plan for each quarter Recruit, hire and develop a team of Account Executives as the team grows Coach the team on deal strategy, forecasting and pipeline generation, and set a high bar for how we sell Build senior relationships with managing partners, general counsel, CIOs, chief innovation officers and knowledge management leaders Lead and support the largest deals through firm-wide pilots, partner committee review, security and confidentiality review, procurement and close Help firms move from pilots to firm-wide rollouts and expand across practice groups and offices Partner with Product, Marketing, Solutions and Customer Success to shape legal use cases, content, messaging and customer outcomes Bring a clear view of the legal AI market back to leadership and Product Deliver accurate forecasts and keep pipeline and account records current in Salesforce Qualifications 10+ years of enterprise SaaS sales experience, including 4+ years leading quota-carrying sales teams Track record selling to large law firms and corporate legal departments, with relationships you can bring to the table Experience in legal tech, legal research or AI, and a real understanding of how legal AI is evaluated and adopted Proven record of building or scaling a team or vertical and meeting or exceeding the number in a high-growth environment Fluent in how legal organizations buy, including innovation teams, partner sponsors, pilots, ethical walls, data security and client confidentiality requirements Strong recruiter of sales talent with a network across legal tech and AI Clear, credible communicator with senior partners, GCs and executives Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience Nice to have Experience at a fast-growing legal AI company or a major legal research provider Experience selling to both law firms and in-house legal teams JD or prior legal practice experience Experience building a vertical team at an early-stage or high-growth company",
