    "summaryAr": "About the Team The Cloud Platform Infrastructure team builds, defines, and manages the foundational infrastructure blocks and standards powering ClickHouse Cloud end-to-end. We own the core backend infrastructure where ClickHouse instances live, while also building the internal platform, tooling, and abstractions that empower all ClickHouse engineering teams and new acquisitions to ship seamlessly. We are expanding o",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Team The Cloud Platform Infrastructure team builds, defines, and manages the foundational infrastructure blocks and standards powering ClickHouse Cloud end-to-end. We own the core backend infrastructure where ClickHouse instances live, while also building the internal platform, tooling, and abstractions that empower all ClickHouse engineering teams and new acquisitions to ship seamlessly. We are expanding our team in the US to balance our global footprint alongside our European engineers and are looking for a seasoned, self-driven Senior Software Engineer to help lead our US operations, drive self-service platform capabilities, and scale our multi-cloud architecture. What You Will Do Architect & Scale Multi-Cloud Infrastructure: Design, deploy, and maintain robust, fault-tolerant distributed infrastructure across hundreds of clusters and thousands of nodes in a multi-cloud, multi-region environment (AWS, GCP, and Azure). Build Self-Service Platform Capabilities: Develop internal tooling, abstractions, and automated workflows that empower other engineering teams to self-serve their infrastructure needs, significantly reducing operational bottlenecks and manual intervention. Drive Automation & GitOps: Build cloud-native platform services and automating resource management Lead Security & Migration Initiatives: Execute mid- to long-term infrastructure migrations and champion security-first engineering initiatives to harden our cloud environments against emerging threats. Optimize Observability & Reliability: Partner across ClickHouse engineering teams to improve system observability and debug complex production issues at scale. Participate in Working-Hours On-Call: Join a predictable, rotating on-call schedule (approximately one week every other month) strictly limited to your local working hours, collaborating with regional counterparts for smooth global handoffs. About You Experience at Scale: Relevant software engineering or platform infrastructure experience building and operating large-scale, stateful, fault-tolerant distributed systems (e.g., managing hundreds of clusters, dozens of cloud accounts, or thousands of nodes). Strong Programming Foundation: Proficiency in Go and/or Python (with familiarity in Bash), demonstrating a developer-first mindset for building reliable services and automation rather than manual operations. Kubernetes Mastery: Deep experience operating and developing on managed Kubernetes services. Public Cloud & IaC Expertise: Hands-on production experience with major public clouds (strong preference for AWS and/or GCP ) and Infrastructure-as-Code tools such as Terraform , Terragrunt , and Atlantis . GitOps & CI/CD Tooling: Proven experience managing deployments and cluster configurations using GitOps workflows and tools like ArgoCD and Helm . Ownership & Collaboration: High level of accountability and autonomy, strong production debugging skills, and a passion for collaborating across a globally distributed engineering organization to solve complex infrastructure challenges. Perks Flexible work environment - ClickHouse is a globally distributed company and remote-friendly. We currently operate in over 25 countries. Healthcare - Employer contributions towards your healthcare. Equity in the company - Every new eligible team member who joins our company receives equity. Time off - Flexible time off in the US, generous entitlement in other countries. A USD$500 Home office setup if you’re a remote employee. Global Gatherings – We believe in the power of in-person connection and offer opportunities to engage with colleagues at company-wide offsites. Culture - We All Shape It As part of a rapidly scaling start-up, you will be instrumental in shaping our culture. Are you interested in finding out more about our culture? Learn more about our values here . Check out our blog posts or follow us on LinkedIn to find out more about what’s happening at ClickHouse. Equal Opportunity & Privacy ClickHouse provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type based on factors such as race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Please see here for our Privacy Statement.",
