    "summaryAr": "About the Team Business Marketing helps knowledge workers, developers, and business decision-makers understand and adopt OpenAI’s products, supporting both self-serve growth and our managed sales team. Our creative work makes complex capabilities clear, grounded, and human as they move from the lab into businesses and everyday work. About the Role We’re looking for an experienced Art Director to develop and direct cr",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Team Business Marketing helps knowledge workers, developers, and business decision-makers understand and adopt OpenAI’s products, supporting both self-serve growth and our managed sales team. Our creative work makes complex capabilities clear, grounded, and human as they move from the lab into businesses and everyday work. About the Role We’re looking for an experienced Art Director to develop and direct creative for OpenAI’s business audiences. You’ll turn product capabilities, customer insights, and marketing briefs into visual ideas that can carry a campaign across channels. That might mean developing the visual concept for a launch, storyboarding a film about how a customer uses AI in their work, or building a campaign system that holds together across a landing page, paid social, and a keynote. This is a hands-on role. You’ll sketch concepts, build key visuals, and set the visual direction for designers, producers, and external partners. You’ll work closely with writers, Business Marketing, Product Marketing, and product teams to make sure the work is accurate, useful to the audience, and unmistakably OpenAI. To us, creativity is a team sport. Ideas get better when you talk them through and build on each other’s thinking. We value curiosity over certainty, kindness over ego, and the ability to balance craft with decisiveness. In this role, you will: Lead visual concept development and art direction for B2B campaigns, product launches, customer stories, and industry events, from brief through final production. Partner with writers and marketers to define the idea around a specific audience, what they need to understand, and what we want them to do next. Work with product and technical partners to show how capabilities work in practice, using product imagery, demos, diagrams, and motion without overstating what the technology can do. Develop campaign visual systems that adapt to different formats and audience needs, from a launch film or event keynote to a product page, paid campaign, or sales presentation. Art direct photography, illustration, motion, and video. Make work yourself when the project calls for it, and give clear direction to internal teams and external partners when others are producing it. Maintain a high visual bar across touch points and help evolve how the OpenAI brand shows up for business audiences. You might thrive in this role if you: Have 8+ years of art direction or related creative experience in-house, at an agency, or both, with a portfolio that shows your role in developing concepts and taking them through production. Have experience creating work for business or technical audiences, with examples of making a complex product, service, or idea clear and compelling. Bring strong visual design fundamentals in typography, composition, imagery, and systems, and can apply them across digital, social, film, and experiential work. Can build a strong campaign idea and show how it adapts across formats without losing what makes it distinctive. Can explain your creative decisions to marketing and product partners, work through feedback, and make sound tradeoffs when priorities or timelines change. Nice to Have Experience with AI, enterprise software, developer tools, or other emerging technologies. Experience art directing customer stories, product demos, or keynote and event creative. Motion design, video art direction, or on-set experience. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
