    "summaryAr": "About Ramp Ramp is building the smart infrastructure for finance teams, embedded in the transaction flow of every dollar a business spends. We automate how over $275B in annualized spend flows in and out of 85,000+ companies: authorizing payments, flagging risk, categorizing spend, and closing books. The problems are high-stakes, data-dense, and unforgiving. We hire people with high agency and high urgency. We look f",
    "descriptionAr": "About Ramp Ramp is building the smart infrastructure for finance teams, embedded in the transaction flow of every dollar a business spends. We automate how over $275B in annualized spend flows in and out of 85,000+ companies: authorizing payments, flagging risk, categorizing spend, and closing books. The problems are high-stakes, data-dense, and unforgiving. We hire people with high agency and high urgency. We look for slope over intercept. We care less about where you trained and more about what you’ve built. At Ramp, everyone is a builder who owns problems end to end and makes consequential decisions that shape the outcome. The median Ramp customer saves 7.5% and grows revenue 16% in their first year – far in excess of businesses operating without Ramp. We believe every ambitious company deserves the same. If you want to build systems that directly shape how companies move and manage billions, Ramp is the place to do it. About the Role Ramp is hiring a Manager, CSM, New Products to build and lead the team that helps customers put our newest products to work. This team supports customers across segments. Its job is to take a new product from sales handoff through implementation, first useful result, and early adoption, then make sure the next owner has a clear path forward. The products and customer needs will change. You will build a team and an operating rhythm that can change with them. You will coach people with different strengths, help them make good decisions when the playbook is still being written, and turn what we learn from customers into a better way to launch the next one. You will work closely with Sales, core Customer Success, Solutions, Product, and Operations to make the customer experience feel coordinated. What You'll Do Hire, onboard, coach, and develop a growing team of Customer Activation Managers. Set a clear bar for customer judgment, implementation ownership, follow-through, and communication. Give direct, useful feedback through customer-call reviews, case discussions, one-on-ones, and development plans. Help strong individual contributors grow into broader scope and address performance gaps early. Help the team turn an unclear sales handoff into a customer plan with the right stakeholders, prerequisites, owners, milestones, and first useful outcome. Step in on complex launches and escalations when your judgment will move the work forward. Build and improve the team's implementation process: assignment and handoff, customer discovery, launch plans, specialist engagement, first-use checks, adoption follow-up, and the transition to ongoing ownership. Make ownership clear when a customer has both a core Customer Success Manager and a New Products specialist. Keep one customer plan while giving the specialist room to lead the product implementation. Use customer progress, launch quality, team capacity, and time spent on implementations to spot where customers or team members are getting stuck. Adjust coverage and process based on what the data and customer work show. Partner with Sales, Product, Solutions, Support, and Customer Success leaders to resolve recurring blockers, set realistic customer expectations, and improve product readiness and the next launch. Bring early customer patterns back to Product and leadership. Be specific about what customers can do today, what takes specialist help, and what we need to change before the motion scales. Build a team culture where people take ownership, ask for help early, share what they learn, and keep improving the work. What You'll Need Either 2+ years directly managing a customer success, implementation, solutions, or consulting team or 6+ years as an individual contributor in one or more of those roles, with clear evidence that you have coached others and led work beyond your own accounts. A record of taking customers through a complex implementation or workflow change, from discovery and planning to first use and adoption. You know how to tell whether a customer is actually using what was launched. Experience building or improving a process that other people used, with examples of what you changed after seeing it work in practice. Strong coaching judgment. You can diagnose whether someone needs clearer expectations, better skills, more support, or a change in approach, and you can give feedback that improves performance. Comfort making coverage and prioritization decisions with incomplete information. You can balance customer complexity, team capacity, and product readiness without losing sight of the customer's outcome. The ability to work across Sales, Product, Solutions, and Customer Success when ownership is shared or a customer issue has no obvious answer. Clear communication with customers, individual contributors, and senior leaders. You can explain a risk, make a recommendation, and identify the next owner and step. Curiosity about new products and enough technical and finance fluency to ask good questions, challenge a launch plan, and bring in the right expert. You do not need to be the specialist for every product the team supports. Nice to Haves Experience building a new post-sale team or launching an implementation motion before the playbook was mature. Experience supporting both high-touch implementations and lighter-weight activation paths across different customer segments. Experience with finance software, accounting workflows, developer-facing products, or AI-assisted customer workflows. Experience using customer and team data to improve coverage, coaching, and implementation quality. Benefits available to all full-time Ramp employees (Global) Flexible PTO Centralized home-office equipment ordering Health and wellness stipend Budget for intra-office travel Weekly coffee stipend United States 100% medical, dental & vision insurance coverage for you, with partial coverage for dependents One Medical annual membership 401(k), including employer match on contributions made while employed by Ramp Fertilit",
