    "summaryAr": "GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster. The same principles built into our products are r",
    "descriptionAr": "GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster. The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. Co-create the future with us as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software. * Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab. An overview of this role As an Executive Assistant at GitLab, you’ll help two senior leaders protect time for their priorities. You’ll primarily support a Vice President in Product and also support a Vice President in Marketing. You’ll manage both executives’ calendars, travel, and expenses. This all-remote role is open to candidates in the United States and Canada, with no preference for a specific time zone within those countries. What you’ll do Manage both executives’ calendars across time zones, resolving scheduling conflicts before they disrupt priority meetings. Prepare a complete itinerary for each domestic or international trip, including flights, hotels, and any required visas. Submit and reconcile expense reports for both executives by each reporting deadline, following GitLab’s travel and expense policies. Coordinate recurring leadership activities with the Senior Executive Business Partner and keep shared office resources, distribution lists, Slack channels, and calendars up to date. Plan team events, offsites, and large meetings with partners across GitLab so schedules and logistics are in place before each event. Use artificial intelligence (AI) tools like Claude to capture meeting notes and reduce manual note-taking while protecting confidential information. Cover for other Executive Business Administrators by handling time-sensitive calendar, travel, and expense requests before they’re due. What you’ll bring Experience providing executive-level administrative support to multiple senior leaders at once and adapting to each leader’s needs. Proficiency with productivity, video meeting, team messaging, and travel and expense tools, and the ability to learn new tools quickly. We use Google Workspace, Zoom, Slack, and Navan. Experience with comparable tools, such as Microsoft Teams for messaging, is welcome. Sound judgment under pressure: you can work independently, stay composed when plans change, and know when to reprioritize or escalate competing executive requests. Experience planning offsites or comparable events, with the organization, clear communication, and attention to detail to coordinate with multiple teams. Experience using AI to improve day-to-day operations while keeping sensitive information confidential. Ability to build relationships and gather context remotely, with flexibility in your working hours to coordinate across regions. Experience supporting teams across offices or regions can transfer to this role. Ability and willingness to travel domestically and internationally to support executives, offsites, and key events. Expect roughly one trip per quarter on average, though frequency will vary. Experience supporting Product or Design leaders, or working at a software company or startup, is helpful but not required. We welcome candidates from different backgrounds and value transferable experience. About the team The Executive Business Administration team helps GitLab’s leaders work effectively in an asynchronous environment. We work with teams across GitLab to coordinate leadership meetings, maintain shared resources, and bring people together for events. You’ll partner with our Senior Executive Business Partner and other Executive Business Administrators. How GitLab will support you Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being Flexible Paid Time Off &nbsp; Team Member Resource Groups Equity Compensation &amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan Growth and Development Fund Parental leave &nbsp; Home office support Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from underrepresented groups are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you're excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application. The base salary range for this role’s listed level is currently for residents of the&nbsp;United States only. This range is intended to reflect the role's base salary rate in locations throughout the US.&nbsp;Grade level and salary ranges are determined through interviews and a review of education, experience, knowledge, skills, abilities of the applicant, equity with other team members, alignment with market data,&nbsp;and geographic location.&nbsp;The base salary range does not include any bonuses, equity, or benefits. See more information on our benefits and equity . Sales roles are also eligible for incentive pay targeted at up to 100% of the offered base salary. United States Salary Range $78,400 &mda",
