    "summaryAr": "OpenAI’s Go-to-Market (GTM) organization helps customers adopt and scale our AI products. As the business grows, we’re looking for a strategic operator to lead high-impact GTM programs that improve execution across the organization. In this role, you’ll work directly with sales leaders to turn their business priorities into programs their teams can run. You’ll partner with Product, Marketing, Product Marketing, Opera",
    "descriptionAr": "OpenAI’s Go-to-Market (GTM) organization helps customers adopt and scale our AI products. As the business grows, we’re looking for a strategic operator to lead high-impact GTM programs that improve execution across the organization. In this role, you’ll work directly with sales leaders to turn their business priorities into programs their teams can run. You’ll partner with Product, Marketing, Product Marketing, Operations, Enablement, Finance, and Communications to take those programs from strategy through execution. You’ll bring structure to ambiguous problems and build repeatable processes that help the business scale. What you’ll do Lead high-priority GTM programs, including product launches, sales plays, and customer initiatives. Partner with sales leaders to identify gaps in pipeline and agree on which programs to run. Work with frontline managers to put those programs into practice and review results. Build program plans with clear owners and milestones. Keep teams aligned through regular reviews and concise executive updates. Use pipeline and productivity data alongside customer and field feedback to inform decisions and improve program outcomes. Build repeatable processes that help teams plan, launch, and measure programs across the GTM organization. We’re looking for 8+ years of experience in Sales Programs, Strategy & Operations, Business Operations, Program Management, Management Consulting, Product Marketing, or a related field. Experience working directly with enterprise sales leaders as a business partner. You’ve helped a sales leader identify a growth opportunity, built a program their reps used, and measured its impact on pipeline or revenue. A track record of leading complex cross-functional initiatives from strategy through execution. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to bring clarity to ambiguous business challenges. Clear communication and experience influencing senior leaders across functions. The ability to manage competing priorities and take ownership of results in a fast-paced environment. Nice to have Experience in a high-growth SaaS, AI, platform, or enterprise technology company. Experience building operating models, planning cadences, launch processes, or executive reporting. Familiarity with product launches, customer engagement programs, or product-led growth. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
