    "languages": [],
    "summaryAr": "Grafana Labs is the company behind Grafana Cloud, the fully managed observability platform trusted by more than 10,000 organizations to ensure reliability, resolve incidents faster, and optimize telemetry at scale. Built on open source and open standards and designed for interoperability across any stack, Grafana Cloud brings AI to observability and observability to AI, giving teams (and their agents) unified visibil",
    "descriptionAr": "Grafana Labs is the company behind Grafana Cloud, the fully managed observability platform trusted by more than 10,000 organizations to ensure reliability, resolve incidents faster, and optimize telemetry at scale. Built on open source and open standards and designed for interoperability across any stack, Grafana Cloud brings AI to observability and observability to AI, giving teams (and their agents) unified visibility so they can see, understand, and act on all their disparate data, wherever it lives, and move at the speed of their ambitions. Customers, including Anthropic, Bloomberg, NVIDIA, Microsoft, and Salesforce, rely on Grafana Labs. We are a 100% remote company with team members across 40+ countries, backed by leading investors including Lightspeed Venture Partners, Sequoia Capital, GIC, Coatue, J.P. Morgan, CapitalG, and Lead Edge Capital. Learn more at grafana.com and follow us on LinkedIn and X . We’re scaling fast and staying true to what makes us different: an open-source legacy, a global collaborative culture, and a passion for meaningful work. Our team thrives in an innovation-driven environment where transparency, autonomy, and trust fuel everything we do. You may not meet every requirement, and that’s okay. If this role excites you, we’d love you to raise your hand for what could be a truly career-defining opportunity. The Opportunity: We’re looking for a Strategic Partnerships Lead to own multi-threaded strategic partnerships and carry those negotiations from structuring through signature and into the field. This is a senior individual contributor role. It is not a program role. You will work with two kinds of partners: Large, publicly traded ISVs, where one relationship covers the product integration, the commercial agreement, and how both field teams take it to customers. And developer and infrastructure platforms, where you will expand our one-click motion: a customer clicks “Monitor with Grafana Cloud” in the partner product, we create or attach a Grafana Cloud account, and telemetry, dashboards, and alerting are provisioned without a manual setup. You will recruit partners, work closely&nbsp; with Product and Engineering teams on what gets built, negotiate the terms that make the integration hold, and work with Sales so the partnership shows up in real pursuits.&nbsp; This role reports to the Senior Director, Corporate Business Development. What You’ll Be Doing: - Own the plan for each partner, including which opportunities to pursue and which to pass on - Scope product integrations with Product and Engineering, including one-click provisioning into Grafana Cloud, the telemetry and dashboards that come with them, and where Grafana shows up inside the partner product - Lead negotiations through signature, covering revenue share, attribution, placement, co-sell, data and brand terms, and term length - Run integration, commercial, and field workstreams together on large ISV partnerships, so a term in one workstream still works in the others - Expand the “one-click” motion to additional partners, and structure the economics around the product surfaces that drive conversion - Launch partnerships with the field, including enablement, account mapping, and a path for sellers to use the integration in a pursuit - Coordinate Product, Engineering, Sales, Marketing, Finance, and Legal from the first structuring conversation through launch What Makes You a Great Fit: - You have owned technology partnerships end to end, including the negotiation, with more than one live workstream in the same account - You have closed integration partnerships that Product and Engineering had to build, and the commercial terms held after signature - You have taken a partnership into the field, including the launch and seller enablement - You are comfortable running several significant negotiations at the same time - You work across Product, Engineering, Sales, Legal, and Finance without needing a team under you - 8-10+ years in strategic business development, product partnerships, or technology alliances Bonus Points For: - Partnerships in developer tools, infrastructure, observability, or API platforms - Experience with large, publicly traded ISVs, including who owns the roadmap and who owns the field - In-product distribution: placement, provisioning or marketplace motions, and revenue share tied to conversion - Enough technical fluency to work with engineers on APIs, telemetry, and account provisioning - Structuring experience in corporate development, strategy, legal, or finance In the United States, the OTE (on target earnings) range for this role is $ 183,857 - $ 220,629 . Actual compensation may vary based on level, experience, and skillset as assessed throughout the interview process. All of our roles include Restricted Stock Units (RSUs), giving every team member ownership in Grafana Labs' success. We believe in shared outcomes—RSUs help us stay aligned and invested as we scale globally. *Compensation ranges are country specific. If you are applying for this role from a different location than listed above, your recruiter will discuss your specific market’s defined pay range &amp; benefits at the beginning of the process. Why You’ll Thrive at Grafana Labs: 100% Remote, Global Culture -&nbsp; As a remote-only company, we bring together talent from around the world, united by a culture of collaboration and shared purpose. Scaling Organization – Tackle meaningful work in a high-growth, ever-evolving environment. Transparent Communication – Expect open decision-making and regular company-wide updates. Innovation-Driven – Autonomy and support to ship great work and try new things. Open Source Roots – Built on community-driven values that shape how we work. Empowered Teams – High trust, low ego culture that values outcomes over optics. Career Growth Pathways – Defined opportunities to grow and develop your career. Approachable Leadership – Transparent execs who are involved, visible, and hum",
