    "languages": [],
    "summaryAr": "About the Team Dots for Companies helps organizations put AI to work. Our scope includes increasing adoption and retention in Business and Enterprise plans, exploring shared AI teammates with their own responsibilities, and building the tools people need to manage their work. We build on the broader Dots platform while developing experiences specific to companies. About the Role We are looking for Senior and Staff Fu",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Team Dots for Companies helps organizations put AI to work. Our scope includes increasing adoption and retention in Business and Enterprise plans, exploring shared AI teammates with their own responsibilities, and building the tools people need to manage their work. We build on the broader Dots platform while developing experiences specific to companies. About the Role We are looking for Senior and Staff Full Stack Software Engineers to build Dots product experiences from the interface through the services that power them. You will help define how people delegate tasks to enterprise agents, follow their progress, and collaborate with them over time. This role combines hands-on product development with the systems work needed to make persistent, asynchronous agent experiences reliable. In this role, you will: Build full stack experiences that help teams discover, adopt, and continue using Dots at work. Develop workflows for shared AI teammates, including how people assign responsibilities, inspect work, and give feedback. Build management and observability experiences that help users understand what Dots are doing and how well they are performing. Partner on enterprise identity, permissions, and connector experiences so users understand what a Dot can access and which identity it acts under. Turn open questions into focused experiments, ship useful increments, and use feedback and product data to guide iteration. Own application architecture and production quality across the features you ship. Work independently across team boundaries to resolve dependencies and keep projects moving. You might thrive in this role if you have: Experience shipping user facing software across frontend and application backend systems, with clear ownership of the resulting user experience. Strong product judgment: you can explain the user problem, the tradeoffs you made, and what changed after launch. Systems thinking that connects interface behavior, APIs, data models, integrations, and operational needs. The ability to make progress when requirements are incomplete, seek the right input, and adjust as you learn. Interest in AI tools that help people do work, with a willingness to experiment with unfamiliar product patterns. A collaborative approach and clear communication about decisions, dependencies, and results. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
