    "summaryAr": "About the Role On OpenAI’s Cyber Partnerships team, you’ll help partners across the Americas build red-team and purple-team services that improve customer defenses. You’ll represent Daybreak in the partner community, showing security teams how to use AI for cyber defense and how to secure AI systems. You’ll work with practice leaders and sellers at systems integrators, managed security service providers, and speciali",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Role On OpenAI’s Cyber Partnerships team, you’ll help partners across the Americas build red-team and purple-team services that improve customer defenses. You’ll represent Daybreak in the partner community, showing security teams how to use AI for cyber defense and how to secure AI systems. You’ll work with practice leaders and sellers at systems integrators, managed security service providers, and specialist firms to turn customer needs into services their practitioners can deliver repeatedly. In this role, you will Build red-team and purple-team offerings with partners. Package fixed-scope red-team assessments and recurring purple-team exercises. Define what customers buy, what partners deliver, and where Daybreak supports the work. Be Daybreak’s go-to partner speaker. Through partner events, live demos, and workshops, show practitioners how to use AI for cyber defense and how to secure the AI systems they deploy. Set delivery standards for partner red- and purple-team engagements. Help partners scope authorized engagements, agree on success criteria with customers, and verify improvements in detection and response after fixes. Turn partner ideas into pilots and product proposals. Lead early customer pilots with partners and bring recurring delivery needs and lessons from those pilots to Daybreak Product. Grow paid Daybreak usage through partner services. Work with partner sellers and OpenAI account teams to help customers move from an initial assessment to recurring purple-team engagements. Partners earn service fees for delivery. Customers generate paid Daybreak usage when they use it to validate fixes and run follow-on exercises. You’ll own offer design, practitioner enablement, and partner pilots. Partners sell and deliver the services. Partner Engineering owns integrations, technical validation, and deployment support. Cyber Partnerships leads partner strategy and commercial commitments. You might thrive in this role if you have Hands-on experience in authorized security testing, with depth in red teaming and experience working with defenders to improve detection, response, or remediation. Experience building or launching repeatable security services, with an understanding of how to price, staff, and deliver them consistently. The ability to explain technical security concepts to buyers and practitioners through customer conversations, demos, workshops, or training. Experience helping customers adopt a new security or AI product and applying lessons from early deployments to later engagements. The ability to build trust with partner leaders and work across sales, engineering, and product teams. Preferred experience Familiarity with AI models and their harnesses, including how the surrounding software supplies tools and context and enforces permissions. What success looks like Partners launch, sell, and repeatedly deliver red-team and purple-team offers. Customers continue using Daybreak after the initial engagement, generating paid usage through fix validation and follow-on exercises. Customers can verify improvements in detection and response, and lessons from pilots inform Daybreak product decisions. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
